   "l": "Knowing the abiding — capacious;",
   "v": true,
   "i": "To know what abides is to have room for everything;",
   "n": "Five short units follow, each three characters, each taking the last one's predicate as its own subject: capacious → impartial → whole → heaven → the Way → lasting. Every link is the one word 乃 'and then, and so'; the line after the last rung, 沒身不殆, steps off the ladder and has no 乃. Warring States writers loved this ladder form; it looks like a proof and works like a chant. That the units are this short is not our doing — the sense-units of this text are the places where Wang Bi's commentary breaks into it, and here he stopped at every rung."
